                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "75a738b7-3857-4337-8cf5-4720bff1345a",
                                "sense_id": "3b88b139-3fdb-363a-8ac9-64916facd327",
                                "text": "16th century, Edmund Spenser, An Hymne Of Heavenly Love\nCompar'd to that celestiall beauties blaze,\nWhose glorious beames all fleshly sense doth daze\nWith admiration of their passing light,\nBlinding the eyes, and lumining the spright"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6ff7982-dba3-4e6c-b7bb-aa03cf8a8501",
                                "sense_id": "3b88b139-3fdb-363a-8ac9-64916facd327",
                                "text": "When canned foods pall, a rifle is a handy bolsterer of the meat supply in this land of wild game; when, in the lonely night, the two geologists have talked through every subject in their ken, a book lumined by a gasoline lamp is a real diversion."
                            }
